This project uses AGENTS.md as the single source of truth for agent instructions.

Read AGENTS.md first, then load context on demand from .agents/ as its routing tables direct.

Rule files in .agents/rules/ carry `description` and `globs` frontmatter so they can be
auto-attached by path. Do not duplicate rules into this file — it exists only so Cursor
finds the entry point.

Note: Cursor's modern form is .cursor/rules/*.mdc. This file is the legacy-but-supported
equivalent and is kept as a single pointer rather than a duplicated ruleset.
